00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:27.320
You see a strong theory was at the end of R2, it was Lelouch who was driving this cart here.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.320
Now what you didn't know is that if we zoom in on the cart here,

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:33.080
uh, zoom in a bit closer, and just enhance it a bit,

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:36.900
we can quite clearly see that Sunrise had planned this all along.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.360
And you know, they were obviously waiting for just the right moment to spring this on us.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.640
BUT HEY, THAT'S JUST A THEORY.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.480
AN ANIME THE-

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:54.180
*dramatic music*

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.940
Alright, let's take a step back for a second and have a serious talk about this.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.560
I'm sure that a lot of us remember Code Geass fondly as

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.420
the anime that grabbed the entire community nearly a decade ago,

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:06.080
and this announcement has come with very mixed feelings.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.560
Some of you are hyped as hell at the prospect of more Code Geass,

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:11.400
and some of you are very worried about the prospect of a continuation,

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:13.500
of which I am definitely in the latter camp.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.080
Don't get me wrong, I love Code Geass and if this turns out to be a great sequel,

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:18.340
fucking brilliant!

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.840
But we have to wonder what the true purpose is of Sunrise

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.720
making a continuation to one of their most beloved anime franchises.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:27.060
Whether this was something that was planned out that can actually properly work,

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:28.340
or just a quick cash-grab.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:31.480
Which considering how well the ending wrapped up everything in the second season,

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:36.400
and how a direct continuation was quite unnecessary, a lot of us are afraid it's going to be.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.520
We can only speculate at this point as there is minimal information about it,

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:41.940
and whatever side you're on, it's best to keep an open mind as

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.460
Yes, this is actually happening!

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:48.340
Personally, I remain hopeful, but catious of the possibility of this continuation tarnishing

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:52.900
one of the most conclusive and, in my opinion, one of the best anime endings regardless of-

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.160
Inner Gigguk: Oh god, what happened to the writing in the middle of this season?!

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.080
And I would've preferred it if Sunrise just pulled a Gundam

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.840
and just continued the timeline without rehashing the main character.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:02.260
Yes, if it sucks, we can just pretend it didn't exist,

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.380
but I love the charm of the original ending was not knowing

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:07.760
whether Lelouch truly did die sacrificing himself for the greater good and-

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.800
Inner Gigguk: Sunrise, are you going to tell me that this epic ending was all for nothing in the end?!

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:12.540
In conclusion, JIBUN WO?

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.660
More like JIBUN woah, calm down guys, let's wait and see how this plays out

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:19.300
'cause it could suck, but you know, it could be good too.

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:20.220
Hopefully.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:20.900
Maybe.

